  "reason": "R1 and R10 identify the accuracy and transferability of empirical interatomic potentials as a problem in closely related refractory multicomponent alloys and connect potential choice to short-range-order predictions. R5, R12, and R17 provide only broad support for including additional thermodynamic or electronic contributions to phase stability. None of the records proposes an MTP, FEP as a replacement for thermodynamic integration, exploitation of low MTP–DFT energy-difference variance, or the DOS-gap electronic correction. Thus the records motivate a more accurate computational treatment but leave the central MTP-plus-FEP intervention and its detailed mechanism as substantial new ideas."
